<title>USA: U.S. factory vegoil product use - Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. factory vegoil product use - Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. factories used 1,123.9 million lbs of vegoils in August in edible product output versus a revised 1,209.8 million lbs in July and 1,256.8 in August 1995.</p>
<p>U.S. factory vegoil use with refining losses were as follows:</p>
<p>   (Mln Lbs) --   Aug 96   July 96     Aug 95</p>
<p>    Soybean Oil  1,161.0     994.7-R   1,081.2</p>
<p> Cottonseed Oil	N/A	N/A	    N/A</p>
<p>Year-to-date oil use with refining losses (Mln Lbs):</p>
<p>				    1996	   1995</p>
<p>		 Soybean Oil   8,279.8	8,407.5</p>
<p>	    Cottonseed Oil	 N/A	    N/A</p>
<p> OUTPUT -- Soybean Crude  10,606.8     10,332.3</p>
<p>		     Refined   8,008.9	8,132.8</p>
<p>	  Cottonseed Crude     918.2	    N/A</p>
<p>		     Refined     594.3	  664.9</p>
<p>		  Corn Crude   1,390.2	1,504.6</p>
<p>		     Refined     637.5	  736.9</p>
</text>
